   $q$How does Text 2 change the way the lesson is learned compared with Text 1?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The speaker never learns the lesson, while the pine learns it immediately after the first strong wind.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"The speaker learns in one race and tells it in first person, while the pine learns over seasons in a third-person fable.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Both characters learn the lesson from a long speech given by an older and wiser character.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The speaker learns the lesson before the race begins, while the pine learns it before summer.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-plot"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The speaker learns in one race and tells it in first person, while the pine learns over seasons in a third-person fable.$q$, $q$The fable spans summer, autumn, snow and spring and is told from outside, while the poem covers one race in the speaker's own "I." The oaks "said nothing" and the coach "just nods," so no long speech appears.$q$, 'draft', 'cce15e04-4a2f-5fc0-9fc3-dd9a766dd461')
