insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('6eab32cd-f96d-51dd-9ce2-29799fbb0156', 'rg9-comparing-texts-p08', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g9-comparing-texts'), null,
        '9-12', $q$Keeping the Record$q$, $q$Text 1: The Copyist of Amberfall (an invented legend)

In the invented city of Amberfall, the oldest book in the library had begun to fade. Its ink was turning the color of weak tea, and each year another page became impossible to read. A young copyist named Idris Moreau asked the librarians for permission to save it. Every morning for three years, he sat by the tall window and copied one page onto fresh paper, line by line, even the spots where an earlier hand had made mistakes.

When he finished, the librarians placed the new copy beside the old one. Visitors asked why he had not corrected the mistakes. "Because they belonged to the person who wrote them," Idris said. "My job was to carry the book forward, not to make it mine."

Text 2: The Mill Tapes (a poem that retells the legend)

My great-uncle talks, and I record
the clatter of the looms he ran,
the whistle at the seven o'clock shift,
the lunch pail and the coffee can.

He mixes up the year it closed.
He calls one foreman by two names.
I do not fix them as I type.
I let his memory stay the same.

The mill is apartments now, and brick,
the river quiet where it turned.
But in the folder on my desk
are forty pages, all he learned.

I am not writing my own book.
I'm only carrying his along,
the way a copyist keeps the ink
exactly where it once belonged.$q$, 'draft')
