   $q$Text 2 includes details such as the mill becoming apartments and the river growing quiet. What do these details add that Text 1 does not emphasize?$q$, $q$[{"text":"They show that the river caused the mill to close, which is the main lesson of the poem.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-cause-effect"},{"text":"They show that the great-uncle's memories are false, since the mill never really existed.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"They show that the speaker wishes the mill had never closed and plans to reopen it someday.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"They show that the place itself has vanished, so the record may be the only remaining trace of that way of life.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They show that the place itself has vanished, so the record may be the only remaining trace of that way of life.$q$, $q$In Text 1 the old book still sits beside the copy, but in Text 2 the mill is gone, which raises the stakes of preserving the great-uncle's words. The poem never says why the mill closed, so the cause-and-effect choice is unsupported.$q$, 'draft', '6eab32cd-f96d-51dd-9ce2-29799fbb0156')
